    "title": "Lisa Ann Ray - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago Lisa Ann Ray passed away June 14, 2025 at Heart to Heart Hospice in Spring, Texas. She was born in Worland, Wyoming, Nov. 5, 1954 to Archie and Merle (nee Phillips) Ray. Lisa was raised in Powell, Wyoming, and loved gymnastics, softball and sports in general until she was in a car accident at age 15. She loved cards, especially poker and bridge. Her car accident caused numerous surgeries through the years. Lisa graduated from Powell High School in 1973 and went on to earn her BSN nursing degree from the University of Wyoming in 1980. She worked as a nurse in Powell, Laramie and Midland, Texas. Lisa met Jim Cozzens in Powell in February 1976 and they married in the Presbyterian Church in Powell in 1982. Lisa and Jim drove into Rome the summer of 1982 when Italy won the World Soccer Cup that year. They spent three months in Spain, France, Switzerland, Italy and Greece before moving to Casper, Wyoming. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
